claim=dict(id='c-notify-identity',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='If append_notify completes successfully with an assigned log index, the decided entry at that index must be the entry submitted by that invocation, including when leadership changes between acceptance and notification. Timeout or Superseded is permitted instead of success.',source_ids=['s-notify-contract','s-notify-errors'],scope=dict(description='The captured async runtime over one valid three-node core configuration, distinct comparable entry payloads, no compaction or crash, and real core/runtime messages delivered by the caller. A partition may delay an old leader response while a different quorum elects a new leader and decides a different entry.',assumptions=['Each node has a unique configured id and initially empty MemoryStorage.','Application supplies transport; no messages or state are fabricated or modified.','Success is interpreted at the one-based accepted index returned by the runtime; core read offset is index minus one.'],excluded=['No guarantee that an arbitrary admitted invocation succeeds.','No global consensus agreement violation is asserted.','Crash persistence, reconfiguration, snapshotting and batching are outside this check.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['s-runtime-assignment','s-runtime-forward','s-runtime-drain'],expectation_ids=['s-notify-contract','s-notify-errors'],binding_ids=['bind-notify-drain'],derivation='The public method says append an entry and await its decided log index. The Superseded documentation permits stopping conservatively when a leader changes because the entry might still survive; this permits false-negative errors, not success for another value. Assignment records index and ballot at acceptance, while core consensus may replace unchosen values across ballots. Therefore success requires the requested entry, not solely a decided numeric position.',applicability='Use the original caller invocation, its real tagged EntryId and real assignment; correlate successful response with the live decided log at the same origin.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Superseded or Timeout can satisfy the safety requirement without deciding the input.','If new leader retains the original value, successful notification is consistent with the requirement.']))
